From: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_hnat: skip PPPQ auto-offset for all non-WHNAT external devices

On NETSYS v3 (MT7987/MT7988), IS_PPPQ_MODE only exempted no-ARP external
interfaces (Raw-IP QMI), causing Ethernet-type USB WWAN modems (CDC-ECM
and CDC-NCM) with ARP to receive qid += 12 and fqos/tport_id queue
assignment even when no PPPQ port exists for external USB devices.

Exempt all unclassified non-WHNAT external devices from the automatic
PPPQ qid offset while preserving PPPQ for GMAC/DSA ports, WHNAT/WED
interfaces, and explicit IS_PPPQ_PATH flows.

Signed-off-by: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_nf_hook.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_nf_hook.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_nf_hook.c
index 1234567..89abcde 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_nf_hook.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_nf_hook.c
@@ -4275,11 +4275,11 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	/* An unclassified no-ARP external output has no PPPQ port assignment. */
+	/* An unclassified non-WHNAT external output has no PPPQ port assignment. */
 	if (IS_PPPQ_MODE &&
 	    !(hnat_priv->data->version == MTK_HNAT_V3 &&
 	      qid == 0 && gmac == NR_PDMA_PORT && IS_EXT(dev) &&
-	      hnat_dev_is_noarp_ext(dev) && !whnat &&
+	      !whnat &&
 	      !IS_PPPQ_PATH(dev, skb))) {
 		qid+= gmac;
 		if (gmac == 0) qid+= 12;
-- 
2.43.0
